# Component Structure

## Directory Layout
```
src/components/
  ui/          # shadcn/ui primitives re-exported (Button, Input, Dialog, etc.)
  layout/      # Header/, Footer/ — structural layout components
  shared/      # Cross-feature reusable components (ProductCard, Rating, Badge)
  features/    # Feature-scoped components
    products/  # ProductGrid, ProductFilters, ProductDetail
    cart/      # CartDrawer, CartItem, CartSummary
    checkout/  # CheckoutForm, AddressForm, OrderSummary
    reviews/   # ReviewCard, ReviewForm, StarRating
    admin/     # DataTable, AdminSidebar, CrudModal
```

## File Naming
- One component per file, named `ComponentName.tsx` (PascalCase).
- Index file `index.ts` in each folder for clean imports.
- Companion types in `src/types/`, styles via Tailwind only.

## Component Template
```tsx
'use client'; // only if needed

import { cn } from '@/lib/utils/cn';
import type { ComponentNameProps } from '@/types/...';

export function ComponentName({ prop1, prop2 }: ComponentNameProps) {
  return (
    <div className={cn('base-classes', { 'conditional-class': condition })}>
      {/* content */}
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Rules
- Single responsibility — one component does one thing.
- No inline styles — Tailwind utility classes only.
- Use `cn()` for all conditional/dynamic class composition.
- Prefer composition: build complex UI by composing small focused components.
- Export named functions (not default exports) for better refactoring.
- Keep component files under 200 lines; extract sub-components when needed.
- Reuse shadcn/ui primitives before creating custom alternatives.
